This is the second time I hit the Nightmare level.  The first time, I 
found it demanding but the fun way.  It took me very long to figure out 
the way to the left side of the level, I was almost killed by two air 
elementals and I had a very suspenseful fight with the (master) mind 
flayers Mel C., Victoria and Ginger (Ginger should actually be Geri or 
Victoria Posh...), whom I did not allow to get close enough to me to 
touch me.  Nightmare was difficult, because ray attacks won't help and 
she is hitting hard, but doable (with a submachine gun).

This time, things are quite different and annoying.  The level is 
infested with giant fleas, ticks and lice that keep multiplying as they 
are killed.  I don't think this will stop after having killed 255 each, 
I must have already done that...  In the meantime they even have almost 
filled up the level containing the magic portal...  Because I need room 
to fight Nightmare, I finally retreated.  A way to get rid of them would 
of course be to genocide them.  But that would take three scrolls of 
genocide, if I don't want all other "a" to go, too. (They are useful on 
the Astral plane, after all.)  If I just fight them long enough, will 
they eventually stop multiplying?  Taming them with charm monster gives 
a little room each time as the tamed ones are "movable" and don't 
multiply.  I might tame a whole 25 by 25 square using confused reading 
of a scroll of taming, but then I only have one of those, so it would 
not solve the problem permanently...

